            <ArticleTitle>Patellofemoral pain: epidemiology, pathophysiology, and treatment options.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>313-27</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.csm.2014.12.011</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0278-5919(14)00131-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients with anterior knee pain present a complex and common problem to health care providers. The diagnosis and treatment of these patients often involve a comprehensive evaluation that includes assessing the chronicity of the pain, the specific location of the complaint, and the previous treatment modalities attempted by the patient. This common diagnosis includes a wide variety of different pathologic abnormalities that can be present independently or concomitantly and cause a spectrum of disabilities for the patient.</AbstractText>
